We have exposed some compute function at the frontend, but the exposed compute function does not support defining the output stride.
  te.def(
      "Compute",
      [](const std::string& func_name,
         const std::vector<ExprHandle>& dim_args,
         py::function func) {

Currently, we always convert the input and output tensor to contiguous regardless of channles-last. So the lowering function does not need the output stride information because it is always contiguous. But the situation will be changed as long as NNC supports channels-last without converting to contiguous. Hence, the lowering function needs to create the output Buf according to the stride information. That's why we need to extend the lowering function and pass the output stride information to it.
Before:
using NNCLoweringFunction = std::function<Tensor(
    const std::vector<ArgValue>& inputs,
    const std::vector<ExprHandle>& outputShape,
    const c10::optional<ScalarType>& outputType,
    at::Device device)>;
After:
using NNCLoweringFunction = std::function<Tensor(
    const std::vector<ArgValue>& inputs,
    const std::vector<ExprHandle>& outputShape,
    const std::vector<ExprHandle>& outputStrides,
    const c10::optional<ScalarType>& outputType,
    at::Device device)>;
